      "writtenOn": "2024-07-11T20:55:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We should send the tarball to `/tmp` and cleanup once it\u0027s unpacked:\n\n```\nTMPDIR :\u003d $(shell mktemp -d)\nTARBALL :\u003d $(TMPDIR)/$(TOOLCHAIN_HASH).tar.zst\n...\ncurl --retry 3 --fail --location --output $(TARBALL) $(TOOLCHAIN_URI) \u0026\u0026\ntar --use-compress-program pzstd --no-same-owner -xf $(TARBALL) \u0026\u0026\nrm -rf $(TMPDIR)\n```\n\nAlternatively, if you encode this using make targets, `make` will automatically clean up intermediates (which would be the typical way to solve this problem).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 9
